      <species id="mw66cf0f21_3c0e_463d_8d72_a573be529e83" name="qPSC" compartment="mwc70ef14b_d309_4431_8c36_e8bc78b4b260" initialAmount="0" substanceUnits="MWUSERUNIT_cell" hasOnlySubstanceUnits="true" boundaryCondition="false" constant="false">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Quiescent pancreatic stellate cells in tumor compartment. In normal pancreas, PSCs store vitamin A and maintain stromal homeostasis.</body>
        </notes>
      </species>
      <species id="mw5751ee55_05d8_4c70_a62f_f90e1f585cad" name="iCAF" compartment="mwc70ef14b_d309_4431_8c36_e8bc78b4b260" initialAmount="0" substanceUnits="MWUSERUNIT_cell" hasOnlySubstanceUnits="true" boundaryCondition="false" constant="false">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Inflammatory cancer-associated fibroblasts. Secrete IL-6 and CXCL12, driving MDSC recruitment, M2 polarization, and CXCR4-mediated T-cell exclusion (Elyada 2019, Ogawa 2021). Driven by tumor-derived IL-1alpha; TGFb antagonizes via IL-1R1 repression.</body>
        </notes>
      </species>
      <species id="mw45623265_442f_4920_87d5_0b25ad67d0ec" name="myCAF" compartment="mwc70ef14b_d309_4431_8c36_e8bc78b4b260" initialAmount="0" substanceUnits="MWUSERUNIT_cell" hasOnlySubstanceUnits="true" boundaryCondition="false" constant="false">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Myofibroblastic cancer-associated fibroblasts. Secrete ECM (collagen), TGFb, VEGF. Build desmoplastic barrier. Favored by TGFb signaling (Biffi 2019). (CXCL12 is iCAF-derived, not myCAF -- audit m2-A-ECM-01.)</body>
        </notes>
      </species>
      <species id="mw1d693e4c_593c_4012_ad5d_b3000e32e957" name="apCAF" compartment="mwc70ef14b_d309_4431_8c36_e8bc78b4b260" initialAmount="0" substanceUnits="MWUSERUNIT_cell" hasOnlySubstanceUnits="true" boundaryCondition="false" constant="false">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Antigen-presenting cancer-associated fibroblasts. Express MHC-II, present tumor antigen tolerogenically -&gt; Treg induction. Rarest subtype ~2-5% of CAFs (Elyada 2019).</body>
        </notes>
      </species>
      <species id="mwa9881b53_c621_4232_b5c7_ffb972d89269" name="collagen" compartment="mwc70ef14b_d309_4431_8c36_e8bc78b4b260" initialAmount="0" substanceUnits="MWBUILTINPREFIX_milli_MWBUILTINUNIT_gram" hasOnlySubstanceUnits="true" boundaryCondition="false" constant="false">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Fibrillar collagen (types I/III) in tumor (total mass in mg). Primary structural ECM component driving desmoplasia. Determines pore size (immune exclusion) and stiffness (mechanotransduction).</body>
        </notes>
      </species>
      <species id="mwad34a05f_7e3b_433d_8d02_b4e0d5d710c7" name="CXCL12" compartment="mwc70ef14b_d309_4431_8c36_e8bc78b4b260" initialConcentration="0" substanceUnits="MWDERIVEDUNIT_nanomolarity_milliliter" hasOnlySubstanceUnits="false" boundaryCondition="false" constant="false">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">CXCL12/SDF-1 chemokine secreted by iCAFs. Major T cell exclusion mechanism in PDAC via CXCR4 signaling (Elyada 2019, Ogawa 2021).</body>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <SimBiology xmlns="http://www.mathworks.com">
            <Unit Numerator="nanomolarity"/>
          </SimBiology>
